common#:#webfolder_instructions_info#:#The webfolder instructions are shown on browsers, which can not open a webfolder directly. You can use HTML code, and the following placeholders: <b>[WEBFOLDER_TITLE]</b>, <b>[WEBFOLDER_URI]</b>, <b>[WEBFOLDER_URI]</b>, <b>[WEBFOLDER_URI_KONQUEROR]</b>, <b>[WEBFOLDER_URI_NAUTILUS]</b>, <b>[ADMIN_MAIL]</b>, <b>[WINDOWS]</b>...<b>[/WINDOWS]</b>, <b>[MAC]</b>...<b>[/MAC]</b>, <b>[LINUX]</b>...<b>[/LINUX]</b>. Clear the field to get the default instructions.
common#:#webfolder_instructions_text#:#<p>Follow the instructions below, to open <b>[WEBFOLDER_TITLE]</b> as a webfolder:</p>[WINDOWS]<h3>Instructions for Windows Vista</h3><ol><li>Press the key combination Windows+E to open Windows Explorer.</li><li>Click on 'Add Network Place' in the toolbar.<br/>The 'Add a Network Place' wizard will open.</li><li>Click at the link 'Connect to a website'.</li><li>Select the 'Choose Another Network Location' option, and select 'Next'.<li>In the 'Internet or Network Address' field enter<br/><b>[WEBFOLDER_URI]</b><br/>then select 'Next'.</li><li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.<br/>Repeat this step until you get to the next dialog window.</li><li>Enter a name for the webfolder, then select 'Next'.<li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.<br/>Repeat this step until you get to the next dialog window.</li><li>Select 'Finish'.</li><li>You can now access the webfolder from the start menu 'Computer'.</li></ol><h3>Instructions for Windows XP</h3><ol><li>Press the key combination Windows+E to open Windows Explorer.</li><li>Choose the menu 'Extras &gt; Add Network Place...'.<br/>The 'Add a Network Place' wizard will open.</li><li>Click at the link 'Connect to a website ...'.<br/>The assistant window will open.</li><li>Select 'Next'.</li><li>Select the 'Choose Another Network Location' option, and select 'Next'.<li>In the 'Internet or Network Address' field enter<br/><b>[WEBFOLDER_URI]</b><br/>then select 'Next'.</li><li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.<li>Enter a name for the webfolder, then select 'Next'.<li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.</li><li>Select 'Finish'.</li><li>This will open the webfolder. You can later access the webfolder from the start menu 'Network places' again.</li></ol>[/WINDOWS][MAC]<h3>Instructions for Mac OS X</h3><ol><li>Open the Finder</li><li>Choose the menu 'Go &gt; Connect to Server...'<br/>The 'Connect to Server' dialog will open.</li><li>In the address field enter the following address:<br/><b>[WEBFOLDER_URI]</b><br/>and select 'Connect'.</li><li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.</li></ol>[/MAC][LINUX]<h3>Instructions for Linux with Konqueror</h3><ol><li>Start the Konqueror browser</li><li>In the address field enter the following address:<br/><b>[WEBFOLDER_URI_KONQUEROR]</b></li><li>Press the Enter key.</li><li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.</li></ol><h3>Instructions for Linux with Nautilus</h3><ol><li>Start the Nautilus browser</li><li>In the address field enter the following address:<br/><b>[WEBFOLDER_URI_NAUTILUS]</b></li><li>Press the Enter key.</li><li>Enter your login and password, and select 'OK'.</li></ol>[/LINUX]<p>If opening the webfolder does not work, please contact <a href="mailto:[ADMIN_MAIL]">[ADMIN_MAIL]</a>.</p>
